      "shortDescription": "Mankenberg develops and manufactures self-acting control valves for pressure and level control. Its portfolio includes pressure-reducing and back-pressure valves, vacuum breakers, venting valves, steam traps, float valves, filters, separators and surge-relief equipment.",
      "fullDescription": [
        "Mankenberg GmbH is a German industrial-valve manufacturer founded by Gustav Mankenberg in 1885 and based in Lübeck. The company develops standard and customised self-acting control valves, including compact deep-drawn stainless-steel designs that operate without an external energy supply.",
        "Official product and catalogue sources document pressure-reducing, back-pressure and differential-pressure control valves, vacuum breakers and vacuum-control valves, bleeding and venting valves, steam traps, float valves, surge-relief valves, strainers, filters and separators. These components serve water supply, food and beverage, pharmaceutical and chemical processing, conventional and renewable energy, oil and gas, shipbuilding, offshore, mining, machinery and pulp-and-paper applications."
      ],
